**memory.hpp defines `utils::memory` allocation and pointer-validation APIs.**

## Interface

`memory::allocator` exports `~allocator()`, `clear()`, `free(void*)`, `free(const void*)`, `allocate(size_t) -> void*`, templated `allocate<T>() -> T*`, `allocate_array<T>(size_t) -> T*`, `empty() -> bool`, and `duplicate_string(const std::string&) -> char*`.

`memory` exports static `allocate`, `allocate<T>`, `allocate_array<T>`, `duplicate_string`, `free`, `is_set`, `is_bad_read_ptr`, `is_bad_code_ptr`, and `get_allocator() -> allocator*`.

## State

`allocator` guards `pool_` (`std::vector<void*>`) with `mutex_` (`std::mutex`); `memory::mem_allocator_` is the shared static allocator.